  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Primary runtime path",
      "items": [
        "Input videos ? batch controller ? media stages ? FFmpeg ? MP4/M4A files.",
        "The controller calls analysis and cut generation before audio extraction; modules share its Python process.",
        "FFprobe checks for audio and duration. FFmpeg detects silence, encodes cuts, and copies AAC into M4A."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust crossings",
      "items": [
        "Input media and output folders are operator-selected filesystem paths. Native executables are resolved through PATH.",
        "Boxes mark process and external-service boundaries, not enforced security groups. No sandbox or privilege isolation is configured in the inspected entry points.",
        "Transcription delegates model retrieval to faster-whisper; truststore enables OS certificate trust. Model service/cache behavior is documented in transcrever_audio/README.md:22."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Optional transcription",
      "items": [
        "The root pipeline stops after extraction. The dashed handoff requires a separate transcrever_audio command.",
        "One model is reused per batch; CPU/int8 is the default, CUDA is optional. VAD is enabled unless --no-vad is set.",
        "The transcription CLI writes Markdown; faster-whisper returns segments. Local model-cache details are delegated to the dependency."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Outputs and failure handling",
      "items": [
        "The editor also writes timing TXT files. The controller writes relatorio_pipeline.json after each video, including errors and skips.",
        "Existing media files are protected unless --overwrite is supplied; only cuts from the current run enter extraction.",
        "Video failures allow the batch to continue. No automatic resume; interrupted work can leave partial files. Optional NVENC affects video encoding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence scope",
      "items": [
        "Analyzed the current working tree, including uncommitted runtime modules; upstream HEAD is ce27b9ce8d469118059bbc616234ea74893148fd.",
        "Citations resolve against an isolated local source snapshot bf73dce075bf970397f420cbc878d27dd6b1062d, not an upstream commit.",
        "Changed paths: README.md; deleted root transcrever_audio.py. Untracked runtime paths: pipeline.py, pyproject.toml, edicao_video/, extracao_audio/, transcrever_audio/. Other untracked paths: tests/, .gitignore, .python-version, uv.lock."
      ]
    }
  ]
